---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
---

<DocShell
   title="MCP tool reference"
   summary="Tool names, inputs, browser behavior, and resource URIs for clients connected to a11ied's local MCP server."
   links={docsLinks}
>
   <section class="split panel">
      <div class="stack">
         <div class="panel-head">
            <p class="panel-kicker">Runtime</p>
            <h2>What MCP exposes</h2>
         </div>
      <p>
         The server provides read-only standards resources plus tool calls for criterion lookup,
         applicability inspection, driver actions, and axe scans. It uses the same runtime as the CLI.
      </p>
      </div>
      <div class="split-aside">
         <div class="tag">No second implementation</div>
         <p class="aside-note">
            MCP tools wrap the same runtime functions as the CLI commands.
         </p>
      </div>
   </section>

   <section class="ledger">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Tool families</p>
         <h2>Available tools</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="route-list">
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Driver</strong><span><code>driver_session</code>, <code>driver_action</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Axe</strong><span><code>run_axe</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>WCAG</strong><span><code>wcag_lookup</code>, <code>wcag_levels</code>, <code>wcag_search</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Inspect</strong><span><code>inspect</code></span></div>
         <div class="route-row"><strong>Diagnostics</strong><span><code>doctor</code></span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
         Driver actions are bundled into <code>driver_action</code>. Provide <code>action</code> and
         any required fields such as <code>key</code>, <code>text</code>, or <code>label</code>.
         Use <code>focus</code> with <code>appName</code>, <code>bundleId</code>, <code>processName</code>,
         <code>pid</code>, or <code>windowTitle</code> to bring the right window to the front.
      </p>
      <p>
         <code>run_axe</code> requires exactly one selector: <code>criterion</code>,
         <code>level</code>, or <code>ruleIds</code>. Use <code>include</code> to return only selected
         axe result categories.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Startup</p>
         <h2>Start the stdio server</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>npx -y a11ied mcp</code></pre>
      <p>
         Configure your MCP client to run that command over stdio. The server does not open a
         network port.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="panel">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Resources</p>
         <h2>Read-only resource URIs</h2>
      </div>
      <ul>
         <li><code>a11ied://targets</code></li>
         <li><code>a11ied://wcag/criteria/&lt;version&gt;</code></li>
         <li><code>a11ied://wcag/levels/&lt;version&gt;</code></li>
         <li><code>a11ied://wcag/coverage/&lt;version&gt;</code></li>
      </ul>
   </section>

   <section>
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Behavior</p>
         <h2>Which tools open a browser or control a screen reader</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         WCAG knowledge tools read local data. <code>doctor</code> probes the host environment and can
         run a short recording check on macOS. <code>inspect</code> fetches the requested URL, while
         <code>run_axe</code> opens it in browser automation. Driver tools create sessions and can
         control real assistive technology or a simulated virtual target.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section class="field-note">
      <div class="panel-head">
         <p class="panel-kicker">Before a driver call</p>
         <h2>Open the page for real sessions</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
         For a real driver session, open the page before calling <code>driver_session</code>.
         For a virtual session, pass <code>url</code> to load the document into the simulator.
      </p>
      <p>
         If you omit <code>target</code> on a driver tool, a11ied chooses VoiceOver on macOS,
         NVDA on Windows, or the virtual driver elsewhere. Only pick the virtual target
         when you explicitly want a simulated run, and set <code>allowVirtual=true</code>.
      </p>
   </section>
</DocShell>
